  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "m26-s001",
      "speakerId": "m26-spk-b",
      "startMs": 0,
      "endMs": 5540,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Okay, prep for next week's engineering all-hands. I want the agenda locked today."
    },
    {
      "id": "m26-s002",
      "speakerId": "m26-spk-a",
      "startMs": 5790,
      "endMs": 12470,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "First item should be the good news. JD's promotion to Staff Engineer takes effect July 1."
    },
    {
      "id": "m26-s003",
      "speakerId": "m26-spk-d",
      "startMs": 12720,
      "endMs": 14080,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Congratulations, JD."
    },
    {
      "id": "m26-s004",
      "speakerId": "m26-spk-c",
      "startMs": 14330,
      "endMs": 17590,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Thanks. Mostly it means more architecture reviews."
    },
    {
      "id": "m26-s005",
      "speakerId": "m26-spk-b",
      "startMs": 17840,
      "endMs": 22620,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Second item, branching. We're doing three different things across client repos."
    },
    {
      "id": "m26-s006",
      "speakerId": "m26-spk-c",
      "startMs": 22870,
      "endMs": 27270,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'd push for trunk-based development everywhere. Short-lived branches, feature flags."
    },
    {
      "id": "m26-s007",
      "speakerId": "m26-spk-d",
      "startMs": 27520,
      "endMs": 32300,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Our Gullwing repo is already trunk-based and it's the calmest one."
    },
    {
      "id": "m26-s008",
      "speakerId": "m26-spk-b",
      "startMs": 32550,
      "endMs": 36950,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Then we adopt trunk-based development across client repos. Any objections?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m26-s009",
      "speakerId": "m26-spk-e",
      "startMs": 37200,
      "endMs": 38940,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "None from design."
    },
    {
      "id": "m26-s010",
      "speakerId": "m26-spk-b",
      "startMs": 39190,
      "endMs": 42450,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Decided. I'll present it at the all-hands."
    },
    {
      "id": "m26-s011",
      "speakerId": "m26-spk-a",
      "startMs": 42700,
      "endMs": 46720,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Third item, on-call. The guide is out of date."
    },
    {
      "id": "m26-s012",
      "speakerId": "m26-spk-b",
      "startMs": 46970,
      "endMs": 50990,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'll publish the new on-call guide by July 3."
    },
    {
      "id": "m26-s013",
      "speakerId": "m26-spk-d",
      "startMs": 51240,
      "endMs": 53740,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Include the Lambda rotation, please."
    },
    {
      "id": "m26-s014",
      "speakerId": "m26-spk-b",
      "startMs": 53990,
      "endMs": 55350,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Will do."
    },
    {
      "id": "m26-s015",
      "speakerId": "m26-spk-c",
      "startMs": 55600,
      "endMs": 61140,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Should we put AI code review on the agenda? It's come up again."
    },
    {
      "id": "m26-s016",
      "speakerId": "m26-spk-b",
      "startMs": 61390,
      "endMs": 67690,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "It keeps coming up. We should probably look into that, but not at this all-hands."
    },
    {
      "id": "m26-s017",
      "speakerId": "m26-spk-a",
      "startMs": 67940,
      "endMs": 71580,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Agreed, it's a topic, not a project yet."
    },
    {
      "id": "m26-s018",
      "speakerId": "m26-spk-e",
      "startMs": 71830,
      "endMs": 73190,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Hiring update?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m26-s019",
      "speakerId": "m26-spk-b",
      "startMs": 73440,
      "endMs": 78600,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "We have three open engineering reqs now that the freeze is over."
    },
    {
      "id": "m26-s020",
      "speakerId": "m26-spk-a",
      "startMs": 78850,
      "endMs": 82490,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Add it to the agenda, people will ask."
    },
    {
      "id": "m26-s021",
      "speakerId": "m26-spk-d",
      "startMs": 82740,
      "endMs": 90940,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "One personal request, if we're pairing next week, I'm much better in the afternoons. Mornings I'm on the Gullwing stand-ups."
    },
    {
      "id": "m26-s022",
      "speakerId": "m26-spk-b",
      "startMs": 91190,
      "endMs": 93690,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Fine, afternoon pairing for Kieran."
    },
    {
      "id": "m26-s023",
      "speakerId": "m26-spk-c",
      "startMs": 93940,
      "endMs": 98340,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Pia, while you're out in July, I'll cover team questions."
    },
    {
      "id": "m26-s024",
      "speakerId": "m26-spk-b",
      "startMs": 98590,
      "endMs": 103370,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Thank you, JD. I'll send the handover note before I go."
    },
    {
      "id": "m26-s025",
      "speakerId": "m26-spk-a",
      "startMs": 103620,
      "endMs": 106120,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Anything else for the agenda?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m26-s026",
      "speakerId": "m26-spk-e",
      "startMs": 106370,
      "endMs": 110010,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "A short design demo of the Corvid intake."
    },
    {
      "id": "m26-s027",
      "speakerId": "m26-spk-b",
      "startMs": 110260,
      "endMs": 114280,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Good, five minutes at the end. That's the agenda."
    }
  ],
  "note": {
    "version": 1,
    "body": "# Larkspur engineering all-hands prep\n\n**Date:** June 25\n**Attendees:** Alma Mockwell, Pia Sample, JD, Kieran Testcase, Nell Fixture\n\n## Summary\n\nPia locked the agenda for next week's Larkspur Labs engineering all-hands.\n\n## Agenda\n\n1. **Promotion:** JD's promotion to Staff Engineer takes effect July 1.\n2. **Branching:** adopt trunk-based development across client repos.\n3. **On-call:** the guide is out of date; a new one is coming, including the Lambda rotation.\n4. **Hiring:** three open engineering reqs now that the freeze is over.\n5. **Design demo:** five minutes on the Corvid intake.\n\n## Decisions\n\n- **Adopt trunk-based development across client repos**, with short-lived branches and feature flags. The Gullwing repo is already trunk-based and is the calmest.\n- AI code review stays off the agenda: it keeps coming up, but it is a topic, not a project.\n\n## Action items\n\n- **Pia Sample** — publish the new on-call guide by July 3, including the Lambda rotation; present the branching decision; send a handover note before her leave.\n- **JD** — cover team questions while Pia is out in July.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Kieran is better at pairing in the afternoons; mornings he is on the Gullwing stand-ups.\n- The agenda is final; Pia will circulate it to the whole engineering group before Monday so people can add questions.\n"
  },
